<Project>
  <!--
    Root-level transitive overrides applied to every project in the solution.

    Context: NPOI 1.2.3 is a .NET Framework–era package used transitively by
    the framework. Because it targets only .NET Framework, NuGet falls back to
    the NU1701 compatibility shim but still carries its transitive dependencies.
    Several of those deps conflict with .NET 10 / EF Core 10:

    1. Common.Logging 1.2.0 — .nuspec declares a malformed TFM
       "10 (1.0,Version=v0.0)" that newer NuGet rejects with NU1202.
       Pinned via Include to 3.4.1 (.NETStandard 2.0). NPOI only uses the basic
       LogManager.GetLogger API which is unchanged between 1.x and 3.x.

    2. Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational 1.0.0 — dragged in via
       an old transitive path through NPOI / Quartz 1.x, conflicting with
       EFCore.Sqlite 10.0.4 which requires Relational >= 10.0.4 (NU1107).
       Pinned via Include to 10.0.4. Projects that explicitly reference this
       package (e.g. Core.csproj) will see a NU1504 "duplicate PackageReference"
       warning — this is accepted. NuGet picks the higher version (10.0.4).

    3. Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite 1.0.0 — same ancient transitive
       path as above; conflicts with Test.Mock which explicitly references
       EFCore.Sqlite >= 10.0.4 (NU1107). Pinned via Include for the same reason.
       NU1504 warning accepted.

    WHY Include (NOT Update): Update in Directory.Build.props activates .NET 10
    SDK Central Package Management (CPM) mode. CPM then requires every .csproj
    to omit the Version attribute — but our .csproj files keep explicit versions,
    causing NU1015 errors for all packages on GitHub-hosted runners. Include
    avoids CPM activation; the duplicate-ref NU1504 warning is the accepted
    trade-off. The long-term fix is migrating to Directory.Packages.props (CPM)
    which requires updating every .csproj — out of scope for this CI fix.

    These pins are intentional compatibility overrides (see also
    dependency-management.md § NU1510 for why NU1510 warnings on these
    entries should NOT be treated as "remove me" signals).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Common.Logging" Version="3.4.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="10.0.4" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite" Version="10.0.4" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
